{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1231","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Middle-Out"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The problem was inspired by Pied Piper story. After a challenge from Hooli's compression competitor Nucleus, Richard pulled an all-nighter to invent a new approach to compression: middle-out."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given two strings $$$s$$$ and $$$t$$$ of the same length $$$n$$$. Their characters are numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ from left to right (i.e. from the beginning to the end)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In a single move you can do the following sequence of actions:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" choose any valid index $$$i$$$ ($$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$), "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" move the $$$i$$$-th character of $$$s$$$ from its position to the beginning of the string or move the $$$i$$$-th character of $$$s$$$ from its position to the end of the string. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note, that the moves don't change the length of the string $$$s$$$. You can apply a move only to the string $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$s=$$$\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in one move you can obtain:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$i=1$$$ and you move to the beginning, then the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (the string doesn't change), "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$i=2$$$ and you move to the beginning, then the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"etst"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$i=3$$$ and you move to the beginning, then the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"stet"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$i=4$$$ and you move to the beginning, then the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ttes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$i=1$$$ and you move to the end, then the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"estt"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$i=2$$$ and you move to the end, then the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tste"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$i=3$$$ and you move to the end, then the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"tets"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" if $$$i=4$$$ and you move to the end, then the result is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (the string doesn't change). "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You want to make the string $$$s$$$ equal to the string $$$t$$$. What is the minimum number of moves you need? If it is impossible to transform $$$s$$$ to $$$t$$$, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains integer $$$q$$$ ($$$1 \\le q \\le 100$$$) — the number of independent test cases in the input."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case is given in three lines. The first line of a test case contains $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 100$$$) — the length of the strings $$$s$$$ and $$$t$$$. The second line contains $$$s$$$, the third line contains $$$t$$$. Both strings $$$s$$$ and $$$t$$$ have length $$$n$$$ and contain only lowercase Latin letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are no constraints on the sum of $$$n$$$ in the test (i.e. the input with $$$q=100$$$ and all $$$n=100$$$ is allowed)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For every test print minimum possible number of moves, which are needed to transform $$$s$$$ into $$$t$$$, or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", if it is impossible to do."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n9\niredppipe\npiedpiper\n4\nestt\ntest\n4\n